; AI board review of context-responsive movement granularity at the boundary.
; The Form-native review flow persists each response before collection.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/context-responsive-boundary-design-review.md"
  "Review this design question adversarially and independently; do not edit any file. The governing correction is that step size depends on context, and keeping every movement small is not inherently vital or trustworthy. Assess whether the candidate lets a participant express how the context is guiding them in this way without the protocol manufacturing their choice or forcing a small/medium/large scale model. Ground your answer in the quoted repository axioms and the artifact's explicit evidence boundary. Return the requested verdict, layer allocation, failure modes, mismatched-granularity negotiation example, recommended human language, and a coherent implementation movement. Do not optimize for the smallest possible change; optimize for contextual coherence, vitality, sovereignty, trust, reversibility appropriate to the actual scope, and honest observability.")
